{% from "_macros.j2" import icon %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Privacy, data sources &amp; accessibility – {{ cfg.site.shortTitle }}</title>
<link rel="icon" href="assets/img/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/site.css">
</head>
<body>
{% include "_icons.j2" %}
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
<header class="top"><div class="wrap top-in">
  <a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">D</span><span class="brand-txt"><span class="brand-1">Dudley</span><span class="brand-2">Your MP &amp; your area</span></span></a>
  <nav aria-label="Main"><ul class="nav-list nav-static"><li><a href="index.html">← Back to the home page</a></li></ul></nav>
</div></header>
<main id="main" class="wrap prose" tabindex="-1">
<h1>Privacy, data sources &amp; accessibility</h1>
<p class="muted">Last reviewed {{ built }}</p>

<h2 id="privacy">Privacy notice</h2>
<p><strong>Who runs this site:</strong> {{ cfg.site.runBy }} (contact: <a href="mailto:{{ cfg.site.runByContact }}">{{ cfg.site.runByContact }}</a>). This is an independent information website, not the official website of {{ cfg.mp.name }} MP or the House of Commons. {{ cfg.site.status }}.</p>
<h3>What we collect</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>No forms, accounts or cookies.</strong> This site does not ask for, store or process your name, address, casework or any other personal details. To contact the MP, please use the <a href="{{ cfg.contact.officialRoute }}">official contact details</a>; the MP's office is then responsible for your data.</li>
  <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical information such as your IP address for security purposes. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Map tiles.</strong> The crime map loads only when you press “Show crime map”. It then fetches map images from OpenStreetMap, which will see your IP address. See the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Fonts and scripts</strong> are served from this site itself; we don't use analytics, advertising or tracking.</li>
  <li><strong>Links</strong> to other websites (Parliament, the council, news publishers, social media) take you to sites with their own privacy policies.</li>
</ul>
<h3>People named on this site</h3>
<p>Information about the MP comes from public parliamentary records. Police officer names come from the official data.police.uk neighbourhood team feed. Event details in the diary are published by the MP's office, which decides what is public. If you think something about you should not be here, email us and we'll review it promptly.</p>
<h3>Your rights</h3>
<p>You have rights under UK GDPR, including the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>

<h2 id="sources">Data sources &amp; disclaimer</h2>
<p>The site updates automatically every morning at 07:00 UK time. Each section shows where its information came from and when it was retrieved. If a source can't be reached, the section keeps showing its last good data, clearly dated.</p>
<div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Section</th><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for key, s in d.items() %}
    <tr><td>{{ s.label or key }}</td><td>{% if s.sourceUrl %}<a href="{{ s.sourceUrl }}">{{ s.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ s.source or "—" }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{% if s.status == "ok" %}Updated {{ s.retrievedDisplay }}{% elif s.status == "stale" %}Last good data {{ s.retrievedDisplay }}{% elif s.status == "not-configured" %}Not yet connected{% else %}Awaiting first update{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<ul>
  <li>Parliamentary information is licensed under the <a href="https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/copyright-parliament/open-parliament-licence/">Open Parliament Licence v3.0</a>.</li>
  <li>Police, ONS and other public-sector data are licensed under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>.</li>
  <li>News headlines link to the original publishers; we show only headlines and short summaries supplied in their public feeds.</li>
  <li>Crime statistics cover police neighbourhoods that overlap the constituency, which do not exactly match its boundary.</li>
  <li>Automatic sections are shown as published by the source. They are not commentary, and inclusion of a news story doesn't mean endorsement. We take care, but can't guarantee every figure is complete or current – always check the linked official source before relying on it.</li>
  <li>This site does not use the House of Commons portcullis or any party logo, and contains no party-political campaigning content.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility statement</h2>
<p>We want everyone to be able to use this site. It aims to meet <strong>WCAG 2.2 level AA</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Text and controls meet colour-contrast requirements, and the Atkinson Hyperlegible typeface is designed for readers with low vision.</li>
  <li>Everything works with a keyboard; a “skip to main content” link and visible focus outlines are provided.</li>
  <li>Charts are built as tables with visible numbers, so screen readers can read the figures.</li>
  <li>Images have text alternatives; text can be zoomed to 400% without loss of content; motion is reduced if you ask your device to.</li>
  <li>The site works without JavaScript – the tabs simply show all their content.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Known limitations:</strong> the crime map is visual; the same information is given in the table beside it. Some linked third-party sites may not be accessible.</p>
<p>If you find a problem, please email <a href="mailto:{{ cfg.site.runByContact }}">{{ cfg.site.runByContact }}</a>.</p>
</main>
<footer class="foot"><div class="wrap"><p class="small">Independent information site · not the official website of {{ cfg.mp.name }} MP · run by {{ cfg.site.runBy }}</p></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
